{"id": "lenzing-2026-09-23-004", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lenzing"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Lenzing pivots to premium as specialty fibre supply tightens", "content": "Lenzing is exiting low-margin textile fibres, closing Austria and UK plants and shifting to branded specialty fibres and nonwovens.\nH1 revenue fell 5.5 per cent, but net result after tax more than doubled and free cash flow improved, prioritising margin over volume.\nAsian MMCF rivals are scaling lyocell, while EU traceability rules point to tighter certified specialty supply for mills and brands.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/lenzing-pivots-to-premium-as-specialty-fibre-supply-tightens-313714-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-005", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s textile growth hinges on value addition & automation", "content": "SIMA says India’s textile industry needs higher-value products, automation and diversification to strengthen global competitiveness.\nPalanisamy urged investment in man-made fibres, technical textiles, recycled and sustainable products to tap export opportunities and FTAs.\nCotton price volatility remains a constraint, with cotton making up 65–70 per cent of yarn manufacturing costs.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-textile-growth-hinges-on-value-addition-automation-313710-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-006", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's FY27 GDP growth forecast raised to 7% from 6.6%: S&P Global", "content": "S&P Global raised India’s FY27 GDP growth forecast to 7 per cent from 6.6 per cent, citing stronger-than-expected industrial activity, consumption, exports and government investment. \nIt expects growth to moderate in the second half of the fiscal year as GST rationalisation and tax-cut benefits fade, while forecasting average consumer inflation of 5.1 per cent and a 25-basis-point RBI rate hike.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-fy27-gdp-growth-forecast-raised-to-7-from-6-6-s-p-global-313705-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-007", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Giving yarn packages a digital identity: What it means for mills?", "content": "Barmag presented atmos.io on September 10, 2026, as a smart-factory platform for yarn production, giving each package its own production data.\nThe system links polymer processing, shop-floor data, ERP and warehouse storage to improve mill visibility and detect deviations early.\nUNITEX in Trang Bang, Vietnam is fully digitalised with atmos.io and adds 36,000 tonnes of annual capacity.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/giving-yarn-packages-a-digital-identity-what-it-means-for-mills--313707-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-008", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton eases after sharp rally as export demand weighs", "content": "ICE cotton futures settled lower as traders weighed Monday’s sharp rise, with volume easing to 52,195 contracts.\nUS upland export sales fell 4 per cent week on week to 71,231 bales, while shipments dropped around 20 per cent to 142,076 bales.\nChina’s State Reserve auction sold all 8,049.53 tonnes offered, but the CC Index 3128B and Zhengzhou’s January contract eased.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-eases-after-sharp-rally-as-export-demand-weighs-313706-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
